{"game": "mass-effect-3", "language": "english", "appid": 1238020, "month": "2020-07", "window": 2, "start_date": 1594166400, "end_date": 1594857599, "month_true_total": 115, "quota": 9, "returned": 9, "pulled_at": "2026-10-07 19:51:33 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "72759406", "author": {"steamid": "76561199071506070", "personaname": "Gameout", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199071506070/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 17, "playtime_forever": 9097, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 587, "last_played": 1763165255, "avatar": "5a03974a0b3e9a4ed83fcd7c9172ae4fa814765e"}, "language": "english", "review": "Mass Effect 3 isn't as bad as Steam makes it out to be. Mass Effect 3 is still a good game that has got very good reviews in the past. And also keep in mind that this is still better than Andromeda. Also, games should be reviewed by critics, not the playerbase.", "timestamp_created": 1594857548, "timestamp_updated": 1596268985, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 3, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.523314356803894043", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "72753643", "author": {"steamid": "76561198271825979", "personaname": "Ineptus.Mechanicus", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198271825979/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 2, "playtime_forever": 12090, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 3881, "last_played": 1597522347, "avatar": "9965896f27bdf30a1ae63eefc8baf7e751ddfcdd"}, "language": "english", "review": "we'll bang okay ?", "timestamp_created": 1594848192, "timestamp_updated": 1594848192, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 2, "weighted_vote_score": "0.523809552192687988", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": [{"reaction_type": 17, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 13, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 1, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 2, "count": 1}, {"reaction_type": 21, "count": 1}]}, {"recommendationid": "72751769", "author": {"steamid": "76561197976611058", "personaname": "akumaserge", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561197976611058/", "num_games_owned": 673, "num_reviews": 40, "playtime_forever": 3135, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2107, "last_played": 1615856399, "avatar": "bb9c697db715ad0f901921ad805159d4e373a8f1"}, "language": "english", "review": "Mass Effect 3 is interesting... \n\nThe game itself has a lot of faults compared to the older games, such as in the base game without DLC, you get a very limited amount of characters, there's no hacking minigames when bypassing a door or safecracking a wall safe, there's no planet scanning like in ME2, no resource gathering... There's tons of stuff that makes it feel like they went a step backwards. \n\nOn the PC, it's even worse. Requiring Origin to even play the game which makes it constantly open and close. Audio sometimes not loading after the title screen, very limited graphical setting options inside the game and using the game configure launcher, and the worst of all... still no gamepad support. \n\nIf you want to finish Shepard's story, go ahead get it. It's still great to play as the commander, but don't expect the same ME experience.", "timestamp_created": 1594845757, "timestamp_updated": 1594845757, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.464876025915145874", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "72743534", "author": {"steamid": "76561197961277551", "personaname": "Urban_Epidemic", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/urban_epidemic/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 8, "playtime_forever": 1715, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 864, "last_played": 1596073409, "avatar": "79d3fe5839617eb83a9661071ed021dd56ac8a5b"}, "language": "english", "review": "A great ending to a fantastic trilogy", "timestamp_created": 1594834207, "timestamp_updated": 1594834207, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "72742331", "author": {"steamid": "76561198109718677", "personaname": "Squ1Shy", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198109718677/", "num_games_owned": 369, "num_reviews": 15, "playtime_forever": 720, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 607, "last_played": 1598561184, "avatar": "efc458318c4c2b2fe752cab8c0a42b6d59318099"}, "language": "english", "review": "love it", "timestamp_created": 1594832633, "timestamp_updated": 1594832633, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": "0.476190477609634399", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "72738208", "author": {"steamid": "76561197980957262", "personaname": "Spike", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/Spikeeins/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 124, "playtime_forever": 7014, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 793, "last_played": 1636579844, "avatar": "d0308df494122fb9d42ddb89465a44e44546f794"}, "language": "english", "review": "I don't know, if this was the only game of the series, it'd be okay - but as the last game it's merely \"meh\".\n\nAlthough I can see [spoiler] why the game ends the way it does, it doesn't really satisfy anything. There are more questions created than answered. Some points feel very illogical and are nearly as bad as the personality shift of Liara between ME1 and ME2. \nWhen having a look at what happens at the end, in ME1 Shepard nearly dies, in ME2 Shepard dies right at the beginning - so it's quite logic to end it with him dying (except that one option) in ME3. As said, it isn't a bad ending, I mean you can save all people you were fighting for and only need to sacrifice yourself but... as in ME2 you had really nice squadmates, garrus and tali are simply the best, now you did everything for your friends / lovers but there is no scene where you are taking a dring with garrus, joking with joker - or anything alike.\n\nThats really sad, and a sad ending at least for me.\n\nSo I simply do not recommend it for the plot it offers - I should have played ME1, ME2 and ME3 but not Priority: Earth and just think of my own ending, would've been better :-/[/spoiler]", "timestamp_created": 1594827404, "timestamp_updated": 1594827404, "voted_up": false, "votes_up": 2, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.473032295703887939", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1591887286", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid": "72733887", "author": {"steamid": "76561198007897271", "personaname": "Drcheef", "persona_status": "online", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198007897271/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 25, "playtime_forever": 5689, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, 